course: dictionary
lesson: 15414
title: Squared numbers and areas
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Squared means multiplied by itself. Five squared means 5 × 5, which is 25. We write it with a small 2 after the number: 5². The small 2 tells you how many times to multiply the number by itself.
explain: «The garden is 4 metres squared.» Here squared is used with a unit of area, so it means square metres, written m². It tells you how much flat space the garden covers, not how long it is.
explain: Squared has other meanings too. «Ella drew her graph on squared paper.» Squared paper has small squares printed on it, which helps you draw straight lines and neat shapes. Squared is also the past form of square, as in «He squared his shoulders», which means he straightened them, ready for something.
fact: Squared means multiplied by itself: 3 squared is 3 × 3 = 9.
fact: The small 2 in 5² means 5 × 5 = 25.
fact: Units of area are written squared: metres squared is written m².
fact: Squared paper is paper ruled into small squares.
fact: Squared is also the past form of square, as in «he squared his shoulders».
exercise: What is 4 squared, written 4²? | 44 | *16 | 8 | 2
exercise: «The room is 5 metres squared.» What does metres squared measure? | Height of the ceiling | Weight of the carpet | *Area, the flat space inside the room | Length of one wall
exercise: Which paper has small squares printed on it? | *Squared paper | Lined paper | Tracing paper | Tissue paper
test: «Tom drew a square with sides of 6 cm.» What is 6 squared? | 12 | 3 | *36 | 66
test: Which unit shows area, with a small 2 to show it is squared? | Metres, written m | Metres cubed, written m³ | *Square metres, written m² | Metres, written mm
exam: What is 2 squared plus 3 squared? | 6 | *13 | 10 | 5
